From da55f24173d7d67823ae7ceca638f4e6fb581c8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Agent <agent@localhost>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:59:44 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(ui): control strip above the song list, with a
 message log

The song list column gains a ToolStrip-style bar across its whole width, flush
with the top edge: a shade lighter than the list behind it, with a bottom border
and a hover highlight on every item.

- TopControlPanel: the strip itself. It carries the bell that toggles the log,
  and keeps the room where further items will go.
- AgentJournalPanel: the log, opened by the bell on the right side of the list,
  closed by its own button or Escape. Both themes are honoured. Every entry
  carries its own cross, so a single message can be dropped from the list.
- App.tsx: every message the toast shows is kept as history and handed to the
  log, so a message that flashed past is still readable. Each entry records who
  reported it - the studio itself, or an agent working the window over MCP
  through the `notify` bridge - and the log shows the difference: a robot for the
  agent, a speaker for the studio, with the tone carried by the icon's colour.
  The history is kept in local storage under `messages`, the way the theme and
  the language are, so it outlives a reload; the newest 200 entries are kept.
- i18n: controlPanel, controlPanelMessages, controlPanelMessagesEmpty,
  controlPanelSourceAgent and controlPanelSourceStudio in all five languages.
  The crosses reuse the studio's own `delete` label.

No new runtime dependency, nothing read from disk beyond local storage, and the
desktop build stays self-contained.
